==English==
{{was wotd|2022|October|6}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|upó}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*Heh₃l-|*-mn̥}}
The {{glossary|adjective}} is derived from {{prefix|en|sub|pos1={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘beneath, under’|liminal|t2=of or pertaining to an entrance or threshold}} (from {{der|en|la|līminālis}}, from {{m|la|līmen|t=doorstep, threshold; doorway, entrance; beginning, commencement}}<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=liminal|pos=adj|id=108471|date=March 2022|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|entry=liminal|pos=adj}}</ref> (possibly ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*Heh₃l-|t=to bend, bow; elbow}}) + {{m|ine-pro|*-mn̥|pos=suffix forming action nouns or result nouns from verbs}}) + {{m|la|-ālis|pos=suffix forming adjectives of relationship from nouns}}). The English word is borrowed from {{bor|en|de|subliminal}}, or a {{calque|en|de|unterschwellig|lit=beneath the threshold|t=subliminal|nocap=1}}.<ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|pos=adj.'' and ''n|id=192773|date=March 2022|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=adj}}</ref>

The {{glossary|noun}} is derived from the adjective.<ref name="OED"/>

